<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss short-time work up in February.</title>
<headline>Swiss short-time work up in February.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people affected by short-time work in Switzerland rose to 16,252, up by 1,304 or 8.7 percent from January's 14,948, the Swiss Federal Office for Industry and Trade said.</p>
<p>The number of work hours lost to short-time working rose by 85,118, or 9.1 percent, to 1,016,506 hours, it said.</p>
<p>In January 931,388 hours were lost. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
